30:## 53. I4 — Consumption and Movement
32:A `Moved` leaf cannot be read as if it still contained its previous value. Moving a value does not preserve two copies of an exclusive authority. Initialization state and authority-exercise state are separate checks.
34:## 54. Anchor Ordering and Absence of Orphan Rights
36:`AnchorOrder` and `AnchorOrderHeld` are defined in Section 44. `NoDangling` prohibits an **active** authority from covering a leaf belonging to an unusable place; the invariant does not say that a leaf is initialized. `NoOrphan` requires every active authority held by a place to be connected to a
38:## 55. ArenaInv — Invariant of the Arena Abstraction
40:`ArenaInv` is an invariant of the **library contract**, not an additional predicate of kernel state. For every live arena:
42:- `storage` designates an existing, usable place; the footprint of `internal` is exactly the footprint of `storage`;
43:- `internal` is active, with own mode `Modify`, held by the arena value;
44:- available leaves and issued regions belong to the administered storage;
45:- two still-active issuances have disjoint regions; no leaf of a still-issued region simultaneously belongs to `available`;
46:- every still-issued block authority is a derivative of `internal` complying with exclusivity and validity rules;
47:- anchor and ownership restrictions are respected.

